.TH PYCDLIB-SALVAGE 1 "Nov 2026" "pycdlib-salvage"

.SH NAME
pycdlib-salvage - assess a damaged ISO against its bad-block table and ingest recoverable entries

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pycdlib-salvage [OPTIONS] <iso-file>

.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a tool for triaging an ISO whose medium has reported missing (bad)
logical blocks.  Given the ISO and a bad-block table, it walks the parsed
directory entries, maps each entry's extents to logical blocks, and classifies
every entry as one of:

.TP
.B complete
Every logical block the entry occupies is readable.  A zero-length file has no
data blocks, so it is always complete and is never reported as missing.
.TP
.B partial
A file or symlink payload whose extents include one or more bad blocks.  Only
the blocks on readable media can be recovered.
.TP
.B untrusted
A directory whose own extent includes a bad block.  Entries stored in the bad
block are absent from the parsed listing, so the directory and everything below
it cannot be trusted.

Entries that share an extent (hard links, or the same data exposed through the
ISO9660, Joliet, Rock Ridge, and UDF namespaces) are all affected when a shared
block is bad.  Without \-extract\-to the tool only prints the assessment; with
it, complete entries are ingested to disk while partial files and untrusted
subtrees are skipped unless explicitly requested.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-path\-type " [auto,iso,joliet,rockridge,udf]"
Specifies the path name convention to walk.  Defaults to auto, which prefers
UDF, then Rock Ridge, then Joliet, and finally plain ISO9660.
.TP
.BI \-bad\-blocks " <file>"
Required.  A file listing the unreadable logical blocks as one block number or
inclusive START-END range per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored, and
commas are treated as separators.  Use - to read the table from standard input.
.TP
.BI \-extract\-to " <destpath>"
The local directory to ingest recoverable entries into.  When omitted, only the
assessment report is printed.  Complete files and directories are written using
their ISO paths; entries below an untrusted directory are not written.
.TP
.B \-include\-partial
Also write partial files, zero-filling the bad blocks so surviving blocks keep
their original file offsets.  Partial files are written with a .partial suffix.

.SH SEE ALSO
pycdlib-extract-files(1), pycdlib-explorer(1), pycdlib-genisoimage(1)

